From: Julian Cooper <115541810+Juliansgith@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 01:49:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 29/56] Platoon order bindings return the issued commands, not
 their arguments

AttackTarget, MoveToTarget, MoveToLocation, AggressiveMoveToLocation,
FerryToLocation, LoadUnits, UnloadUnitsAtLocation, UnloadAllAtLocation,
GuardTarget, UseFerryBeacon and UseTeleporter (0x0072FB60 .. 0x00731CB0)
return a table of the commands they issued: each loop takes the
command from its WeakPtr (owner slot - 4), adds 20h -- the command's
CScriptObject::mLuaObj -- and appends it (LuaObject::Insert, 0x00909AF0).
The rebuild inserted CUnitCommand::mArgs, the issue payload, which is an
unbound LuaObject for these orders, so LuaObject::Insert threw
"m_state == obj.m_state" and the calling Lua thread died.

That was every FAF AI platoon that moved, attack-moved, attacked,
guarded or used transports (platoon.lua MoveToLocation, GatherUnits,
platoon-adaptive-guard AggressiveMoveToLocation, ...): it gave its first
order and its AI thread ended there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 75d61853eb39e4f0959e3a010a9488a8d25f2fef)
